From: Razer Edge port draft
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: take mixers for a topology without DSC from the top

On the Razer Edge (SM8350) the DSI panel runs in command mode with DSC
(2 slices, two mixers). With the phone screen on first, the panel gets
LM_0/LM_1 (PP_0/PP_1, DSC_0/DSC_1) and a USB-C monitor plugged in after it
gets LM_2/LM_3: both work. With the screen off when the monitor comes, DP
takes LM_0/LM_1 and the panel, turned on afterwards, lands on LM_2/LM_3,
PP_2 and DSC_2/DSC_3: it never finishes a frame ("frame done timeout",
pp:2, dsi_err_worker) until DP is gone.

Let a topology that needs no DSC search the mixer pairs from the top
(6 7 4 5 2 3 0 1, keeping the even mixer primary), so DP lands on LM_4/LM_5
and the low mixers stay free for the DSC panel. The downstream SDE driver
keeps the same split with qcom,sde-mixer-display-pref (primary first).

Found on the Razer Edge (1 Kasım 2026) from debugfs crtc-N/status in the
good and the bad order.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_rm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_rm.c
index 7e77d88f8..8f3abe86f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_rm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_rm.c
@@ -359,7 +359,14 @@ static int _dpu_rm_reserve_lms(struct dpu_rm *rm,
 	int lm_idx[MAX_BLOCKS];
 	int pp_idx[MAX_BLOCKS];
 	int dspp_idx[MAX_BLOCKS] = {0};
-	int i, lm_count = 0;
+	int i, k, lm_count = 0;
+	/*
+	 * A topology without DSC takes the mixer pairs from the top: the DSC
+	 * encoders bind to the pingpongs of the low mixers, and a DSC panel
+	 * pushed onto LM_2/LM_3 (DSC_2/DSC_3) by a DP sink that came first
+	 * stalls on SM8350 (DSI0 in command mode, frame done timeouts).
+	 */
+	bool from_top = !topology->num_dsc;
 
 	if (!topology->num_lm) {
 		DPU_ERROR("zero LMs in topology\n");
@@ -367,8 +374,10 @@ static int _dpu_rm_reserve_lms(struct dpu_rm *rm,
 	}
 
 	/* Find a primary mixer */
-	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(rm->mixer_blks) &&
-			lm_count < topology->num_lm; i++) {
+	for (k = 0; k < ARRAY_SIZE(rm->mixer_blks) &&
+			lm_count < topology->num_lm; k++) {
+		/* pairs from the top, each pair in order: 6 7 4 5 2 3 0 1 */
+		i = from_top ? ARRAY_SIZE(rm->mixer_blks) - 2 - (k & ~1) + (k & 1) : k;
 		if (!rm->mixer_blks[i])
 			continue;
 
